Part 1: Single Inheritance — Questions 1–5

Single inheritance mein ek child class ek parent class ko inherit karti hai.
Parent class: Vehicle
brand, speed, start()

extends

Child class: Car
fuelType, drive()
-------------------------------------
Q1. Vehicle and Car Management
Medium
Create two classes: Vehicle and Car.
Parent class — Vehicle
- Private fields: brand, speed.
- Constructor to initialize both fields.
- Getters for both fields.
- Method start() that prints "Vehicle started".
Child class — Car extends Vehicle
- Add a private field fuelType.
- Initialize the parent fields using super().
- Create a displayCarDetails() method.
- Call the inherited start() method.
Test: Create a car with brand "Toyota", speed 120 and fuel type "Petrol".



Q2. Method Overriding — Animal Sounds
Medium
Create parent class Animal and child class Dog.
Animal
- Private field name.
- Constructor and getter.
- Method makeSound() prints "Animal makes a sound".
Dog
- Override makeSound() to print "Dog barks".


Q3. Online Order and Express Order
Medium–Hard
Create Order and ExpressOrder.
Order
- Private fields: orderId, orderAmount.
- Validate that the order amount is positive.
- Provide getters.
- Method calculateFinalAmount() returns the order amount.
ExpressOrder
- Private field deliveryCharge.
- Override calculateFinalAmount() to include the delivery charge.
- Reject a negative delivery charge.
- Use super() to initialize the parent.
Test: Order amount ₹2,000 and delivery charge ₹150.
Expected final amount: ₹2,150.
Challenge: If Order has a parameterized constructor but no no-argument constructor, what happens when ExpressOrder doesn't explicitly call super(...)?


Q4. Person → Employee → Manager
Medium
Create three classes:
- Person: private name, age; constructor and getters.
- Employee extends Person: private employeeId, salary; constructor and getters.
- Manager extends Employee: private teamSize; constructor and displayDetails().
Requirements:
- Each constructor must initialize its own fields and parent fields.
- Use super() at the correct level.
- Reject negative age, salary and team size.
- Print all fields using methods.
Test: Akshat, age 25, employee ID 101, salary ₹60,000, team size 5.
Challenge: Does Manager inherit name directly from Person, or through Employee?